              "id": "player-conduct",
              "text": "If an official witnesses any acts of intentional tackling, elbowing, cheap shots, blocking or any unsportsmanlike act, the game will be stopped and the player may be subject to ejection from the game. The decision to eject will be made at the referee’s discretion, which may be determined by the seriousness of the offense or repeated infractions. Once an ejection decision has been made, no appeals will be considered. FOUL PLAY WILL NOT BE TOLERATED!\na.\tPlayers may not physically or verbally abuse any opponent, coach or official.\nb.\tBall-carriers MUST make an effort to avoid defenders with an established position.\nc.\tDefenders are not allowed to run through the ball-carrier when pulling flags."
