              "text": "The visiting team will have possession to start the game. The home team will have first possession in the 2nd half.\nTo start each possession, the ball is always placed on the right hash-mark on the 45-yard line. Once the ball has been advanced, hash-mark placement of the ball must be enforced by officials in accordance with NCAA rules. Offenses always move in the same direction.\nThe field is marked at 15-yard intervals by field striping or with cones. An offense crossing each interval results in a first down. An offense has three downs to cross the 30-yard line, after which it will have another three downs to cross the 15-yard line. Failure to cross each interval in the respective number of downs will result in a change of possession.  Once the offense passes the 15-yard line, it will have four downs to score a touchdown."
